# Server-side list filters

Applies to product list pages (cases inbox, admin users/contractors, contractor cases, …).

## Do

- Filter and page collections on the API (`q` / `query`, `status`, `kind`, `limit`, `cursor` → `nextCursor`)
- Persist active filters in the URL so the result is shareable
- Debounce URL writes (~300ms); fetch from the URL value, not each keystroke
- Paginate with cursor + Load more — do not slice a downloaded array

## Do not

- Client-side `matchesQuery` / `.filter(title.includes)` / status chips over a fetched list
- Refetch on every keystroke
- Drop rows in parsers to fake a server filter

Allowed: hide the current user from a transfer picker; drop `null` parse failures.

If a list needs a new filter, add a query param and a server `where`. No exceptions for “the list is small.”
